Commit 2fd99591, parked on phase/8.4 (tag deleted 2026-10-16)
Subject: fix(web-ui): make every frontend-rendered count name what it counts

Card 31, the screen half. A live TP53 answer showed "78 sources from 3
layers" in the status strip, "of 124 available" in its lead sentence and
"Showing 1 to 10 of 59" in a table pager, three true numbers with nothing
to say which counted what
(testing/Developer/reports/2026-09-20_tp53_findings/findings.md, D-2).
useRunView's status-strip meta now says "N sources cited from M layers",
naming the citation-marker basis rather than a bare "sources". The table
and stacked-list pager's status now names the row kind when the answer's
own record_line label supplies one ("59 disease rows"), falls back to
"records" otherwise, and states the page size alongside the range. The
Sources disclosure's own badge keeps its visible bare-number glyph, per the
design system, and gains an accessible name distinguishing it from the
strip's citation count: a distinct-record count after URL deduplication,
which can legitimately differ from citations cited when one record answers
for more than one marker. No number changed, only what surrounds it.

The backend's own two strings ("of 124 available", "not shown above") are
untouched, per the ticket; the report to the calling builder names what
they should say to match.


